Acknowledgements
--------------------------------------------------------------------------

voxide is an independent work. Its design was informed by the author's prior
work on a fork of the JARVIS voice assistant by Abraham Tugalov
(https://github.com/Priler/jarvis), in particular the general approach of
matching spoken commands to intents using sentence-embedding cosine
similarity with an on-disk vector cache, and the shape of a capability-gated
Lua scripting sandbox for user-authored commands.

No source code from that project is reproduced here. voxide is licensed
independently under MIT OR Apache-2.0; the JARVIS project carries different
licensing terms and no part of it is redistributed with voxide.

--------------------------------------------------------------------------
Third-party model weights
--------------------------------------------------------------------------

voxide does not bundle model weights. `voxide models pull` downloads them at
runtime from their upstream sources, each pinned to an exact revision and
verified by SHA-256. Those models carry their own licenses:

  - Sentence-embedding ONNX models: see the Qdrant FastEmbed model cards on
    the Hugging Face Hub for per-model licensing.
  - Vosk speech recognition models: see https://alphacephei.com/vosk/models
    for per-model licensing (most are Apache-2.0).

Review the license of any model you download before redistributing it or
using it commercially.
